Package: IntrinsicScan
Type: Package
Title: Label-Blind Feature-Wise Intrinsic Binary Partition Scanning
Version: 0.99.3
Authors@R: c(
    person(
        "Leandro", "Altare",
        email = "memedesimo22@gmail.com",
        role = c("aut", "cre"),
        comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0004-5861-8679")
    )
    )
Description: Scans continuous molecular features for intrinsic binary partitions
    using an exact one-dimensional two-medoid objective under L1 loss. Partition
    discovery uses feature values only and is therefore label-blind. Binary
    phenotype labels are used only after the partition is fixed to orient the
    states, quantify phenotype concordance using orientation-free Youden J,
    perform exact conditional inference, and optionally assess resampling
    stability or fixed-partition permutation calibration. The method is intended
    for preprocessed continuous omics measurements and does not claim that a
    fitted partition demonstrates biological bimodality or discrete biological
    states.
